    return best\n16:\n17: # tie/edge cases\n18: cases = ['', 'a', 'aa', 'abba', 'abca', 'abcdef', 'aaaaa', 'pwwkew', 'tmmzuxt',\n19:          'abab', 'abcabcbb', 'bbbbb', 'dvdf', 'abba' + 'xy']\n20: for t in cases:\n21:     got, exp = longest_unique(t), brute(t)\n22:     assert got == exp, (t, got, exp)\n23:     # verify no repeats\n24:     assert len(set(got)) == len(got)\n25:\n26: # random cross-check incl. non-BMP code points and combining/astral chars\n27: alphabet = ['a', 'b', 'c', '😀', '🌍', 'é', '中', '\\U0010FFFF']\n28: for n in range(0, 30):\n29:     for _ in range(200):\n30:         t = ''.join(random.choices(alphabet, k=n))\n31:         got, exp = longest_unique(t), brute(t)\n32:         assert got == exp, (t, got, exp)\n33:\n34: # large performance test: hundreds of thousands of chars\n35: big = ''.join(random.choices('abcdefghij', k=500_000))\n36: t0 = time.perf_counter()\n37: r = longest_unique(big)\n38: dt = time.perf_counter() - t0\n39: assert len(set(r)) == len(r)\n40: assert r == brute(big[:2000] if len(big) > 2000 else big)\n\nSo line 40 is my sanity check: `assert r == brute(big[:2000])`. That's my test's fault, not the implementation's: brute on the 2000-char prefix gives the longest unique substring of the *prefix*, which need not equal the longest unique substring of the full string. That's a flawed sanity assertion. The public test passed and edge cases + random cross-check (6000 random strings incl. emoji) passed, so the implementation is correct.\n\nLet me fix my verification: instead cross-check brute vs sliding window on moderate random strings (e.g. length 2000) directly, and for the big string just measure timing + no-repeat property + length consistency (e.g., that no longer window exists can be checked via the reference on a truncated input). Also remove the invalid assertion.\n\nAlso note: `distinct` string of 1.1M code points — brute isn't applied there, fine.\n\nLet me re-run the verification with the corrected sanity check: cross-check brute vs implementation on random strings of length ~1000 (brute is O(n²) with early break, that's fine), plus timing on 500k."}}
